<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48280" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thyōnē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θυώνη,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the mother of the
				fifth Bacchus</i>, <i>enumerated in</i>
			<i><span class="en">Cic. N.
				D. 3, 23, 58</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thyōneus</span></b> ,
				ĕi, m., <i>the
				son of Thyone</i>, i. e. <i>Bacchus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">indetonsus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					4, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Semeleius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 17, 23</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thyōnĭānus</span></b> ,
				i, m., <i>the son of
				Thyone</i>, i. e. <i>Bacchus</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 13 praef.</span></i>
				—<b>Meton.</b>, for <i>wine</i>, <i><span class="en">Cat. 27, 8</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
